                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6be47753-28d2-39f4-9cfd-a6fa91ced6fb",
                        "entry_id": "79ed0b6a-1083-3f21-b687-eb77d30ed8d6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "концентрированный раствор какого-либо летучего вещества, употребляемый в пищевой, фармацевтической и парфюмерной промышленности"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca56968a-3f3a-4b01-b69c-1987516733ce",
                                "sense_id": "6be47753-28d2-39f4-9cfd-a6fa91ced6fb",
                                "text": "В бидонах были цветочный одеколон, фиалковая эссенция и даже самая лучшая розовая вода."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2a57efe9-029a-3ade-a38b-1d8f60260063",
                        "entry_id": "79ed0b6a-1083-3f21-b687-eb77d30ed8d6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., устар. самое существенное; основа, главная сущность чего-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "085e7e4a-fbfc-4e72-b363-48aeb1875f06",
                                "sense_id": "2a57efe9-029a-3ade-a38b-1d8f60260063",
                                "text": "я, конечно, не хочу утверждать, что здесь шла речь о такой внезапной любви, но определенное ясновидение и вправду здесь было: эту эссенцию Люцииного существа, или — если быть совершенно точным — эссенцию того, чем Люция стала для меня впоследствии, я понял, почуял, увидел разом и с первого взгляда"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "46bcc86e-1f10-486e-b22f-6a179c7f8b95",
                        "source_entry_id": "79ed0b6a-1083-3f21-b687-eb77d30ed8d6",
                        "target_lang_word": "essence",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "essence",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60cda96a-08f4-31a4-901b-61e544455230",
                                        "entry_id": "4b235f6b-e1f4-3b3f-bb5f-0aceaf92b330",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The inherent nature of a thing or idea."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba3e73b3-3456-48f1-9064-57ce9c0f6b4b",
                                                "sense_id": "60cda96a-08f4-31a4-901b-61e544455230",
                                                "text": "CHARITY is a virtue of the heart, and not of the hands, ſays an old writer. Gifts and alms are the expreſſions, not the eſſence of this virtue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "885993cd-883d-430b-a62a-4f5bcda550f1",
                                                "sense_id": "60cda96a-08f4-31a4-901b-61e544455230",
                                                "text": "They [the laws] are at present, both in form and essence, the greatest curse that society labours under ; the scorn of the wicked, the consternation of the good, the refuge of those who violate, and the ruin of those who appeal to them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d22b6da-8e18-46a0-aac2-71bb77fb145c",
                                                "sense_id": "60cda96a-08f4-31a4-901b-61e544455230",
                                                "text": "The essence of Addison’s humour is irony."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74709d15-5bf9-46a7-a42f-e0207de53a00",
                                                "sense_id": "60cda96a-08f4-31a4-901b-61e544455230",
                                                "text": "It may be that a free society as we have known it carries in itself the forces of its own destruction, that once freedom has been achieved it is taken for granted and ceases to be valued, and that the free growth of ideas which is the essence of a free society will bring about the destruction of the foundations on which it depends."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "502948ba-e61e-3a21-b1c1-858854228318",
                                        "entry_id": "4b235f6b-e1f4-3b3f-bb5f-0aceaf92b330",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The true nature of anything, not accidental or illusory."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eaebce59-5f07-30a5-9646-5bbf1ccc3b64",
                                        "entry_id": "4b235f6b-e1f4-3b3f-bb5f-0aceaf92b330",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Constituent substance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5a43e70-38ae-49f3-b568-afbb6098b89b",
                                                "sense_id": "eaebce59-5f07-30a5-9646-5bbf1ccc3b64",
                                                "text": "For Spirits when they pleaſe / Can either Sex aſſume, or both ; ſo ſoft / And uncompounded is their Eſſence pure, / Not ti’d or manacl’d with joynt or limb, / Nor founded on the brittle ſtrength of bones, / Like cumbrous fleſh[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0122826f-47a1-3c45-9cc3-a8243883a945",
                                        "entry_id": "4b235f6b-e1f4-3b3f-bb5f-0aceaf92b330",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A being; especially, a purely spiritual being."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c76200b-dddf-44c2-9e92-10e5b2ccdc19",
                                                "sense_id": "0122826f-47a1-3c45-9cc3-a8243883a945",
                                                "text": "And put to proof his high Supremacy, / Whether upheld by ſtrength, or Chance, or Fate, / Too well I ſee and rue the dire event, / That with ſad overthrow and foul defeat / Hath loſt us Heav’n, and all this mighty Hoſt / In horrible deſtruction laid thus low, / As far as Gods and Heav’nly Eſſences / Can Periſh."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e20f22a-95c8-4526-9091-0fb66c432f0a",
                                                "sense_id": "0122826f-47a1-3c45-9cc3-a8243883a945",
                                                "text": "He [Gottfried Wolfgang] had been indulging in fanciful speculations on spiritual essences, until, like Swedenborg, he had an ideal world of his own around him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7dc3f3f2-9779-3325-8dd5-8c868ef08ddb",
                                        "entry_id": "4b235f6b-e1f4-3b3f-bb5f-0aceaf92b330",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A significant feature of something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3502db39-59d6-388b-8412-9fae06749bf9",
                                        "entry_id": "4b235f6b-e1f4-3b3f-bb5f-0aceaf92b330",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The concentrated form of a plant or drug obtained through a distillation process."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba6d8a92-a27e-42fc-a657-1205e22326e5",
                                                "sense_id": "3502db39-59d6-388b-8412-9fae06749bf9",
                                                "text": "essence of Jojoba"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5d34adfe-98d8-3287-b28d-2d2f9671a0e6",
                                        "entry_id": "4b235f6b-e1f4-3b3f-bb5f-0aceaf92b330",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An extract or concentrate obtained from a plant or other matter used for flavouring, or as a restorative."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44980302-cbe2-4202-a470-1984e10c9789",
                                                "sense_id": "5d34adfe-98d8-3287-b28d-2d2f9671a0e6",
                                                "text": "vanilla essence"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1846bd20-5f0c-49d5-b4eb-50efdefbe572",
                                                "sense_id": "5d34adfe-98d8-3287-b28d-2d2f9671a0e6",
                                                "text": "She bathed the face of the sleeper with some essence, raised her in her arms, and called upon her name."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "205696bb-767d-43a5-b99d-5e85ffb045a1",
                                                "sense_id": "5d34adfe-98d8-3287-b28d-2d2f9671a0e6",
                                                "text": "There was no one to cook the necessary food that the invalids required to pick up their strength; no fowls to be bought, to make into the essence that is so generally given to fever patients wherever I have been since."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e05aeaff-143e-3cf4-b740-c1ed012a491e",
                                        "entry_id": "4b235f6b-e1f4-3b3f-bb5f-0aceaf92b330",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fragrance, a perfume."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e965e32-0735-4388-8423-e0c6cd287baa",
                                                "sense_id": "e05aeaff-143e-3cf4-b740-c1ed012a491e",
                                                "text": "Our humbler province is to tend the Fair, / Not a leſs pleaſing, tho’ leſs glorious care ; / To ſave the powder from too rude a gale, / Nor let th’ impriſon’d eſſences exhale[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
